Gameplay adapted from the mcfish plugin in FloatTech/ZeroBot-Plugin (Go, rules 5.6.2).
Original plugin author: fangliuyu; with contributions from the upstream project.
Upstream: https://github.com/FloatTech/ZeroBot-Plugin/tree/master/plugin/mcfish
Upstream license: GNU Affero General Public License, version 3.
Rod tiers, base durability and prices adapted from:
https://github.com/FloatTech/zbpdata/blob/main/McFish/articlesInfo.json

Modular structure, inventory layout, backgrounds, icons and supplied font reused
from Huanghun542's local astrbot_plugin_mcfishing, supplied with AGPL version 3.
Artwork is preserved from that project; rod and book icons are also copied into
assets/items to provide item-name lookup. Its unknown-item icon is the barrier.

Changes in v2: TypeScript/Koishi reimplementation split into database and core
modules; standalone emerald balance; starter rod and 100 emeralds; configurable
weighted loot table and colors; capped daily casts; 1-40 second batch wait;
two-page warehouse with overflow sale; daily premium buyback; fixed blacksmith;
two enchantments (50%, maximum III); repairs; selective end-of-flow message
recall; persistent fishing recovery; v1 Koishi save migration.
Changes in v2.1: rebalanced default loot values and rarity; half-price buyback;
books excluded from market premiums; one-click sale preserves books and rares;
zero-value rod disposal; persistent platform-local top-ten balance ranking with
masked user IDs, updated usernames and warehouse-background rendering.
Removed shared trading stock, taxes, curses, coupons, synthesis and special tools
from the current game rules. Legacy gear and quantities are preserved on migration.

